ollars raised, though outside groups have spent heavily both supporting and opposing him.\n\nDemocrat Shaun Finnie has out-raised Toth by about two-to-one and earned a Houston Chronicle endorsement as a moderate, and a Democratic-sponsored October poll showed a nine-point race. Prediction markets give Democrats roughly a one-in-three chance, more optimistic than the ratings suggest. The weight of evidence still points to a Republican hold, but by a narrower margin than the district's partisan lean alone would imply.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0698, "margin": -9.59}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0849, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0449, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1331, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0551, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0338, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0241, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0249, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.08, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0526, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0331, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0726, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1087, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0571, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0197, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0502, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0209, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0314, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0454, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.0111, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.045, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.0224, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.0713, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.0127, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-16", "p_dem": 0.059, "margin": -10.2}, {"date": "2026-10-17